.TH SDL_GPUCommandBuffer 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_GPUCommandBuffer \- An opaque handle representing a command buffer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_GPUCommandBuffer SDL_GPUCommandBuffer;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Most state is managed via command buffers\[char46] When setting state using a command buffer, that state is local to the command buffer\[char46]
.PP
Commands only begin execution on the GPU once
.BR SDL_SubmitGPUCommandBuffer
is called\[char46] Once the command buffer is submitted, it is no longer valid to use it\[char46]
.PP
Command buffers are executed in submission order\[char46] If you submit command buffer A and then command buffer B all commands in A will begin executing before any command in B begins executing\[char46]
.PP
In multi-threading scenarios, you should only access a command buffer on the thread you acquired it from\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_AcquireGPUCommandBuffer (3),
.BR SDL_SubmitGPUCommandBuffer (3),
.BR SDL_SubmitGPUCommandBufferAndAcquireFence (3)
